   e_i' = \frac{e_i}{\sqrt{2}}
   \]

   Then the new basis vectors have unit length:
   \[
   \|e_i'\| = \left\| \frac{e_i}{\sqrt{2}} \right\| = \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}
   \]

   Now consider the points:
   \[
   S' = \left\{ \sum_{i=1}^n \alpha_i e_i' : n \in \mathbb{N}, \alpha_i \in \mathbb{R} \right\}
   \]

